      "input_design": "Recipe (standard, modified) applied to whole runs; 3 runs per recipe; 3 wafers per run; 5 exchangeable sites per wafer (90 measurements). Every standard run in chamber A, every modified run in chamber B. Construction: y = 100 + chamber (A 0, B -4) + recipe 0 + run (-1, 0, +1 within recipe) + wafer (-0.5, 0, +0.5 within run) + site (-0.2..+0.2 within wafer).",
      "intended_comparison": "modified - standard (the recipe effect)",
      "demonstrates": "An apparent difference of -4 a.u. that is entirely a chamber difference by construction (the recipe effect is 0). Stratum refuses the comparison, says why more sites cannot fix it, and proposes a crossed randomized assignment with what it would estimate and how precisely.",
