      "input_design": "Etch setting (E1-E4) randomized to wafers, 3 wafers per setting; position (P1-P4, inherent) read once per wafer (48 readings). Construction: y = 50 + alpha (-0.9,-0.3,0.3,0.9) + wafer (-1,0,+1 within setting) + beta (-0.3,0,0.3,0) + gamma (+-0.15 on the E1/E2 x P1/P2 cells) + noise (+-0.3 pattern whose rows and columns sum to 0 within each setting).",
      "intended_comparison": "etch setting, position, and their interaction",
      "demonstrates": "The correct analysis tests etch setting against wafer-to-wafer variation on (3, 8) df and position and the interaction against within-wafer error on 24 df. The naive single-error analysis, shown beside it, calls etch setting significant on 32 df and misses the position effect.",
      "expected_decision": "ANALYZE",
      "expected_findings": [],
      "expected_behaviour": [
        "No warning: equal within-setting spread by construction (SD ratio 1, Brown-Forsythe F = 0) and bounded residuals (largest externally studentized |t| about 1.27 for wafer means and 1.45 for readings).",
        "One report caveat: position is inherent (assignment_not_randomized).",
        "Correct: etch setting F = 1.8 on (3, 8), p > 0.05; MS whole-plot error 4; position F = 8 on (3, 24), p < 0.05; interaction F = 1/3 on (9, 24), p > 0.05; MS subplot 0.09.",
